        "original_id": "a1d1fb52-47e3-5ebb-8767-b112c5c4303c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Herbert Matthews, Fulgencio Batista, Fidel Castro, Ruby Hart Phillips\n- Organizations: The New York Times, 26th of July Movement\n- Places: Sierra Maestra, Cuba\n- Events: Cuban Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Herbert Lionel Matthews was a reporter and editorialist for The New York Times.\n- Fulgencio Batista was the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944.\n- Fulgencio Batista became a U.S.-backed dictator of Cuba from 1952 to 1959.\n- Fulgencio Batista publicly claimed that Fidel Castro had been killed during the 26th of July Movement's landing.\n- Herbert Matthews became notorious after reporting that Fidel Castro was still alive and living in the Sierra Maestra mountains.\n- Ruby Hart Phillips wrote coverage that was relatively favorable toward Fulgencio Batista.\n- Ruby Hart Phillips's reporting was often at odds with that of Herbert Matthews, a noted Times foreign correspondent who favored Fidel Castro.\n- Fulgencio Batista was overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a464d1d4-648f-5654-9463-85c7712b2a00",
        "text": "Page: Herbert Matthews. Sentence: Herbert Lionel Matthews (January 10, 1900 – July 30, 1977) was a reporter and editorialist for \"The New York Times\" who grew to notoriety after revealing that Fidel Castro was still alive and living in the Sierra Maestra mountains, though Fulgencio Batista had claimed publicly that he was killed during the 26th of July Movement's landing.\nPage: Fulgencio Batista. Sentence: Fulgencio Batista y Zaldívar (] ; born Rubén Zaldívar; January 16, 1901 – August 6, 1973) was the elected President of Cuba from 1940 to 1944, and U.S.-backed dictator from 1952 to 1959, before being overthrown during the Cuban Revolution.\nPage: Ruby Hart Phillips. Sentence: Her coverage, relatively favorable toward Batista, was often at odds with that of Herbert Matthews, the noted \"Times\" foreign correspondent who favored Castro.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
